      "kind": "item",
      "label": "A list that only points elsewhere can't be said",
      "excerpt": "A list that only points elsewhere can't be said",
      "text": "Clarify",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-06T23:12:50.818Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-06T23:13:43.121Z",
          "html": "<p>What I34 meant, in plain words:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>PokéAPI's list of pokemon (<code>/pokemon</code>) gives each one's <b>name and address only</b>.  Its height, types, moves ... are at that address, one page per pokemon.</li>\n  <li>When I34 was filed (P18), a program had no way to say so.  It drew the list, and every pokemon in it had a name and nothing else.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>It's fixed now</b>, by P27's line in PokeSpell's <code>PokeSpell.api.spell</code>:</p>\n<pre>- its lists give only each one's \"name\"</pre>\n<ul>\n  <li>The list shows its names at once.  The rest of a pokemon is read from its own address only when something asks for it, e.g. its height, and kept.</li>\n  <li>P34 used the same line for the Met Museum's list of 500,000 ids.</li>\n  <li>The ingest writes the line itself when a server's list is like this.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I'm closing I34 as done in P27.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-06T23:13:39.220Z"
      }
    }
  },
